'''''Cotoneaster microphyllus''''', the '''small-leaved cotoneaster''' or '''rockspray cotoneaster''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Rosaceae]].<ref name="GBIF_3025626" >{{cite web |title=''Cotoneaster microphyllus'' Wall. ex Lindl. |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/3025626 |website=gbif.org |publisher=GBIF Secretariat |author=GBIF Backbone Taxonomy |access-date=7 May 2022 |quote=Small-leaf cotoneaster }}</ref><ref name="MBG_286566" >{{cite web |url=https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=286566 |title=''Cotoneaster microphyllus'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date= |website=Plant Finder |publisher=Missouri Botanical Garden |access-date=7 May 2022 |quote=...commonly called littleleaf cotoneaster... }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Rockspray Cotoneaster |url=http://www.flowersofindia.net/catalog/slides/Rockspray%20Cotoneaster.html |date=2022 |publisher=Flowers of India |access-date=7 May 2022 }}</ref> It is native to the Indian Subcontinent, Tibet, Sichuan, and Yunnan in China, and Myanmar, and it has been introduced to various locales in Europe, Australia, and the United States.<ref name="722578-1" >{{cite POWO |id=722578-1 |title=''Cotoneaster microphyllus'' Wall. ex Lindl. |access-date=7 May 2022 }}</ref> A rabbit-tolerant shrub reaching {{cvt|1|m|ft|0}} tall but spreading to {{cvt|2.5|m|ft|0}}, and hardy in [[Hardiness zone|USDA zones]] 5 through 7, it is recommended for rockeries and hedges.<ref name="MBG_286566" /> Care should be taken not to plant it where it can become invasive.<ref name="MBG_286566" />

